  "published": "2026-09-30T21:10:35.24Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n   1 - Only one response per request: a second WriteAsync / WritePartialAsync / StartChunkedResponseAsync for the same request throws InvalidOperationException. New HttpResponseWriter.HasStarted.\n   2 - HttpHeader and the contentType argument reject CR, LF and other control characters with ArgumentException (prevents response splitting).\n   3 - The keepAlive argument can only narrow the request's choice: keepAlive: true for a request that sent Connection: close now answers Connection: close, and keepAlive: false now closes the connection.\n   Behaviour changes:\n   4 - A handler that writes nothing gets an empty 200; an unfinished chunked response is terminated automatically; an exception after the response started closes the connection instead of appending a 500.\n   5 - Streaming (GetStream / chunked API) to HTTP/1.0 clients uses a close-delimited body instead of chunked encoding.\n   Fixes:\n   6 - Connection header parsed as a case-insensitive token list (\"Close\", \"close, TE\", repeated headers).\n   7 - Header lines without a colon and chunk extensions with control bytes are rejected with 400.\n   8 - Trailers no longer leak into the next keep-alive response; HEAD suppresses body bytes on the writer-level chunked API.\n   9 - Content-Type length included in the response buffer estimate (long values could overrun the buffer).\n   10 - MultipartParser: CRLF-prefixed delimiter, empty parts and header-less parts handled, Content-Disposition parameters matched by name.\n   11 - Range parsing accepts only a single all-digit range.\n   Tooling: CI on Ubuntu and macOS with a Native AOT smoke test; releases published from CI via NuGet Trusted Publishing.",
